# Small-degree representations in defining characteristic
#
# Dimensions and highest weights of irreducible representations of simple,
# simply connected algebraic groups, from Frank Luebeck's tables.
# The data reproduce the overview tables with their stated degree bounds.
# Detailed weight multiplicities and the separately published supplementary
# data sets are not included. The only changes to the overview entries are
# conversion to GAP syntax and the characteristic encoding specified below.
#
# Source: Frank Luebeck, RWTH Aachen University,
# Tables of Weight Multiplicities
# https://www.math.rwth-aachen.de/~Frank.Luebeck/chev/WMSmall/index.html
# Imported from the overview tables on 01-10-2026.
#
# Reference:
# F. Luebeck, Small degree representations of finite Chevalley groups in
# defining characteristic, LMS Journal of Computation and Mathematics 4
# (2001), 135--169, with subsequent extensions published on the website.
#
# Coverage: 51 tables for the following types and ranks.
# A2,...,A20, B2,...,B11, C3,...,C11, D4,...,D11, E6, E7, E8, F4, G2.
#
# Degree bounds (inclusive):
# These are bounds on representation dimension, indexed by algebraic rank.
# The bounds are those of the individual source tables.
# A dash indicates that no table is included.
#
#   Rank       A       B       C       D
#      2     450     300       -       -
#      3    1000    3000    2200       -
#      4    3000    4000    4000   10000
#      5    7000    8000    7000   15000
#      6    9000   15000   10000   20000
#      7   15000   25000   25000   25000
#      8   20000   40000   30000   35000
#      9   30000   50000   40000   70000
#     10   30000   60000   40000   80000
#     11   35000   70000   12000  100000
#     12   40000       -       -       -
#     13   50000       -       -       -
#     14   50625       -       -       -
#     15   65536       -       -       -
#     16  100000       -       -       -
#     17  150000       -       -       -
#     18  130321       -       -       -
#     19  160000       -       -       -
#     20  194481       -       -       -
#
#   E6: 50000, E7: 100000, E8: 500000, F4: 30000, G2: 700.
#
# Data format:
# SmallDegreeTables is a record indexed by type and rank, for example A2.
# Each component is a record with fields
#   bound : the degree bound of the source table
#   rows  : entries of the form [dimension, highestWeight, characteristic].
#
# highestWeight contains the coefficients in the basis of fundamental
# weights, in the order of the source's Dynkin diagram.
# characteristic encodes the Characteristic column as follows:
#   []        all primes
#   [p1,...]  only the listed primes
#   [-p1,...] all primes except the listed primes.
#
SmallDegreeTables:=rec();
